<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Arabic strings for Face MMA.

  Only the strings this locale adds are here. Everything else falls back to
  res/values/strings.xml, which is how the other locales (ru, zh-CN, zh-TW) are
  written too - one English source of truth, one translation per locale, and no
  duplicated copies of the sentences that have not changed.

  The protection control and the responsible-use notice are the reason this file
  exists at all: they are the two places where a mistranslation changes what the
  app PROMISES, rather than only how it looks.

  ⚠ The two endpoint labels must not be swapped. "Least sensitive" is the LOW end
  of the dial and "Most sensitive" is the HIGH end, and the order they appear in
  is checked by a test - a translation that puts them the wrong way round would
  make the slider invert itself for every Arabic reader.

  ⚠ gate_blocked (a mandatory refusal) and gate_blocked_adjustable (a refusal the
  sensitivity setting caused) must stay distinguishable. Collapsing them would
  tell an Arabic reader that a rule they cannot change is something they could
  have changed by moving a slider.
-->
<resources>

